  "worked_solution": "The complement of $S,$ denoted $\\overset{―}{S},$ consists of every element in the universal set $U$ that is not in the set $S.$\n\nThe only elements of $U$ that are not in $S$ are $p,$ $r,$ and $u.$\n\nTherefore, the complement of $S$ is\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{S}={p,r,u}.\n$$",
